# machine-local config: paths + API key. `assets/demars.yaml.example` is the tracked template.
demars.yaml

# run products -- large, machine-specific, and regenerated by the pipeline
runs/
tmp/

# scheduler scratch: per-machine job scripts and the stdout/stderr SLURM drops beside them.
# The tracked, portable templates live in `assets/slurm/`; these are the local copies.
test.j
STDOUT.*
STDERR.*

# Test corpora -- none of it ships, structures or lists. The CIFs are ICSD content, licensed by
# FIZ Karlsruhe under an all-rights-reserved notice. The id lists are not a lighter version of the
# same thing: they name the entries a corpus run measures, and for a held-out set that list IS the
# answer key -- publishing it is how a measurement quietly becomes a lookup. The distribution's own
# test data is `demars-core/tests/fixtures/` (COD, CC0, plus one synthetic cell written here).
testcases/

# Working notes. What ships is the artifact and what it knows -- `episodes/` (the lessons, with the
# provenance that lets the de-identification be audited) and `demars-core/docs/DEFECTS.md` (what every
# D<n> cited in the code means). These two are the notes behind that work, and neither has a consumer
# in the distribution:
#   BACKTEST.md   names which entries are held out -- publishing it would void the backtest rather
#                 than document it.
#   RELEASING.md  the pre-release task list. Each item's OUTPUT ships (the availability wording, the
#                 packaging); the list itself is ours, and it carries a measured fabrication rate,
#                 cost estimates and internal scheduling.
BACKTEST.md
RELEASING.md
